        {
          "text": "Now that we've explored Hughes and Harlem, it's time to apply that same process to a poem of your choice!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Choose one (1) poem from the international poetry collection below and explore how the poet uses sound, language, and structure to communicate something about their experiences identity, or community. ",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each poem's page will have specific instructions or things to consider about that poem and poet. However, regardless of the poem you choose, you'll annotate for things that stick out to you; apply the poetic devices we've learned today; and analyze what the poet might be trying to express in their poem with a 3-5 minute oral analysis. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Your instructor will give more specific instructions for how to turn in your materials, so be sure to ask them for any questions about this portion of the lesson."
